2,Blust - Kiput Historical Phonology-2002,https://www.scribd.com/document/945252681/Blust-Kiput-Historical-Phonology-2002,"The document discusses the historical phonology of the Kiput language, a member of the Berawan-Lower Baram branch of the North Sarawak subgroup of Austronesian languages. It highlights Kiput's unique phonological changes, such as intervocalic devoicing and the spontaneous nasalization of nonlow vowels, which distinguish it from other languages in the region. The study provides a comprehensive ...",Kiput,Austronesian
